---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
const headings = [
  'Before you begin',
  'Install and connect the example',
  'Connect your AI app',
  'Try it',
  'Add an API key',
  'If something fails',
].map((text) => ({ depth: 2, text, slug: text.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ', '-') }));
const config = JSON.stringify(
  {
    mcpServers: {
      blindkit: {
        command: 'node',
        args: [
          '/absolute/path/blindkit/dist/cli.js',
          'serve',
          '--config',
          '/absolute/path/blindkit/blindkit.json',
        ],
      },
    },
  },
  null,
  2,
);
---

<Docs
  title="Make your first connection."
  description="Install Blindkit on your computer and ask your AI to read an example post."
  slug="quickstart"
  headings={headings}
>
  <h2 id="before-you-begin">Before you begin</h2>
  <p>
    This early version uses terminal commands. You need Git to download the code, a current patched
    Node 22 or 24 to run it, and pnpm 10 to install its dependencies. You also need an AI app that
    supports MCP, the standard for connecting AI to tools. To approve changes, that app must support
    MCP approval forms, also called “form elicitation”.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>No database setup.</strong>
    <p>
      Your settings and activity log are saved in files on your computer. Internet access is needed
      for package installation and the public demo API.
    </p>
  </div>
  <h2 id="install-and-connect-the-example">Install and connect the example</h2>
  <p>Download the code, open its folder, then install Blindkit and add the example app:</p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/aliarain/blindkit.git
cd blindkit
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm build
node dist/cli.js init
node dist/cli.js add examples/posts.openapi.json --name posts</code></pre>
  <p>
    This creates your settings file, <code>blindkit.json</code>, and connects JSONPlaceholder, a
    public example API. It can return posts and simulate creating them. Creating a post still asks
    for approval. If a settings file already exists, <code>init</code> leaves it alone.
  </p>
  <h2 id="connect-your-ai-app">Connect your AI app</h2>
  <p>
    Open your AI app’s MCP server settings and add the entry below. Replace both example paths with
    the full path to your Blindkit folder. If the app cannot find Node, replace
    <code>node</code> with the full path to the Node program.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{config}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Restart your AI app or reconnect the server. Blindkit should appear with two tools:
    <code>search</code> finds an action and <code>execute</code> runs it. The settings location
    depends on your AI app.
  </p>
  <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
  <p>
    Ask your AI: “Use Blindkit to find <code>getPost</code> and show me the title of post 1.” The AI
    can use this code:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{'const post = await tools.call("posts.getPost", { id: 1 });\nreturn { title: post.title };'}</code></pre>
  <p>
    You should get the post title back. Reading this example does not need approval by default. You
    can find the activity log at <code>~/.blindkit/audit.jsonl</code>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="add-an-api-key">Add an API key</h2>
  <p>
    The example needs no API key. For an app that does, add a reference to its key in the source’s{' '}
    <code>headers</code> setting:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{'{ "Authorization": "Bearer env://MY_API_TOKEN" }'}</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>env://MY_API_TOKEN</code> names an environment variable: a value supplied to the program
    when it starts. Set that variable through your AI app’s MCP environment settings. Keep the
    actual key out of <code>blindkit.json</code> and AI conversations. Remote apps that receive keys
    must use HTTPS.
  </p>
  <h2 id="if-something-fails">If something fails</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No config found:</strong> check the absolute <code>--config</code> path.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Change was declined:</strong> check that your AI app supports MCP approval forms.
      Review and approve the request before the time limit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Request took too long:</strong> the default is 15 seconds, including approval. Raise{' '}
      <code>limits.timeoutMs</code> up to 120000 if needed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Unsupported spec:</strong> review the{' '}
      <a href="/docs/config/">supported OpenAPI formats</a>. YAML, OpenAPI 3.1, and external
      references are not supported.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Read the <a href="/docs/security/">security guide</a> before connecting an app with private data
    or actions you cannot undo.
  </p>
</Docs>
